# Accepted in the pull request gate of .github/workflows/images.yaml. Scanners still report them, since they go by
# the package version, and so does the Artifact Hub security report.
#
# Django 3.2.25: Taiga 6.10 (and taiga-back main) is pinned to Django 3.2, out of upstream support since April 2024.
# The image applies the security fixes Debian backports to Django 3.2 (django-patches/, see its README).
#
# Fixed in the image by Debian's backports (django-patches/):
CVE-2024-45231
# 0020-CVE-2024-45231.patch
CVE-2025-48432
# 0026-CVE-2025-48432.patch, 0027-CVE-2025-48432-2.patch
CVE-2025-57833
# 0028-CVE-2025-57833.patch
CVE-2025-64459
# 0031-CVE-2025-64459.patch (SQL injection through the _connector argument, critical)
CVE-2026-48587
# 0043-CVE-2026-48587.patch
CVE-2026-48588
# 0042-CVE-2026-48588.patch
#
# Fixed in the image by our backport of the upstream fix (django-patches/9001-CVE-2026-8404.patch):
CVE-2026-8404
#
# Django 3.2 not affected, according to the Debian security tracker:
CVE-2025-64458
CVE-2026-53878
#
# Not reachable in Taiga, not fixed for Django 3.2 by Debian yet:
# GeoDjango (django.contrib.gis): not in Taiga's INSTALLED_APPS, no spatial field or lookup.
CVE-2026-15307
CVE-2026-15830
CVE-2026-53877
# HttpRequest.get_signed_cookie: never called by Taiga or its contribs.
CVE-2026-6873
#
# bleach 4.1.0: taiga/mdrender patches bleach 4 internals (ALLOWED_STYLES, mutable ALLOWED_TAGS) that
# bleach 5+ removed. Neither issue is reachable with Taiga's allow list (no formaction attribute).
GHSA-gj48-438w-jh9v
GHSA-8rfp-98v4-mmr6
